TITLE:: SlcMod
summary:: Adapter for seamless use of Node Proxies as control inputs in SLiCE patterns.
categories:: Live Coding, Patterns
related:: Classes/SLiCE, Classes/Ndef

DESCRIPTION::
Adapter class that promotes the use of Node Proxies as modulators in patterns. As part of the SLiCE live coding environment, it automatically converts an Ndef output to a relevant modulator. From a user perspective, a defined Ndef will be automatically converted to a server side-control or audio rate modulator, or a lang-side OSC modulator where appropriate.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: all
A dictionary of all currently active SlcMods.

METHOD:: initClass

METHOD:: new
Returns a new SlcMod, comprised of an Ndef, a Synth that reads the Ndef's bus and sends the data back to the language.
argument:: key
A unique identifier symbol for the SlcMod (and the Ndef).
argument:: func
The Ndef symth function.
argument:: rate
The update frequency of the reader synth.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: consumers
A List of pattern parameter names that is modulated by this SlcMod.

METHOD:: updateNdef
Private method that updates the embedded Ndef function when the SlcMod is changed and re-run.

METHOD:: replyID
A UniqueID, used by the receiving OSCdef in the SLiCE pattern. Set automatically.

METHOD:: key
The unique identifier symbol of the SlcMod.

METHOD:: oscKey
The unique identifier symbol used by the receiving OSCdef.

METHOD:: init

METHOD:: free
Frees the SlcMod, its embedded Ndef, the reader synth, and the receiving OSCdef.

METHOD:: ndef
Returns the embedded Ndef of the SlcMod.


EXAMPLES::

code::
l = SLiCE(); // start SLiCE

// add a sound of the MIDI instrument type.
// here, assuming a running Korg Polysix plugin, listening on the IAC Driver Bus 1.
// add one or more controllers as an event of (arbitrary) key-value pairs representing
// parameter names and MIDI CC numbers.
(
l.addSound(
	\polysix,
	MIDIEndPoint("IAC Driver", "Bus 1"),
	\stereo,
	nil,
	(p6filterFreq: 34)
);
)

(
Slc(\a,
	\sound, \polysix,
	\ctranspose, Prand([0, -12, 12], inf),
	\note, Prand([0, 3, 5, 8, 10], inf),
	// use the MIDI CC in the pattern and modulate it using a SlcMod.
	\p6filterFreq, SlcMod(\filterLfo, {SinOsc.ar(0.8).range(20, 40)}),
	\reverb, 0.3,
	\reverse, 0,
	\amp, Pwhite(0.4, 1.0),
	\dur, 0.25
).play;
)

Slc(\a).stop
::
